Arara Code: run selected built-in extensions from a writable per-user copy.

Why a patch: icon themes declare resource paths relative to their extension
location, and vscode-icons regenerates manifests in that location. Extension APIs
cannot relocate a built-in before scanning or register icon themes dynamically.
Only product-listed built-ins are copied, preserving their manifest, builtin flag,
identity and version. Atomic publication prevents incomplete concurrent copies;
failures retain the original extension. Copies are isolated by extension and build.
Touches: product.ts, extensionsScannerService.ts, writableBuiltinExtensions.ts.

